From 84f22495735e8414a2d5d4bc419086dc21b80e68 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lordofthepigs <nicolas.piguet@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 21:49:33 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add effect-record instrumentation hooks
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Four hooks an external tool reads to record what each ability does when it
resolves. Every one is inert unless something installs a listener or reads the
pointer, and nothing in Forge does — the reader is a separate project that
builds against stock Forge and reaches these reflectively.

TriggerHandler gains a per-thread pointer to the trigger currently running.
Without it an event that arrives while a trigger resolves is attributed to
whatever else was on the stack, which is wrong exactly when two things resolve
at once. It also gains a listener at the condition evaluation, called with both
answers: a trigger that did not fire is what distinguishes the condition from
the base rate, and it is notified below the mode check so the negatives are
same-event-type candidates rather than every trigger in the game.

ReplacementHandler gains a listener around executeReplacement, the one point
every replacement passes through, called with the parameter map before and
after. The map is deep-copied before the call because replacements mutate it in
place; a shallow copy would show the outgoing values on both sides.

AbilityUtils gains a per-thread pointer to the sub-ability currently resolving,
so an outcome can be attributed to the clause that produced it rather than to
the whole line. Restored rather than cleared on the way out, since a
sub-ability can resolve another.

AiController gains a listener called with the rules-level verdict for each
candidate the AI evaluated — can-play, affordable, has-legal-target. Never the
AI's policy judgment: that is its opinion rather than the game's rules.

GameAction.destroy puts the causing ability in the Destroyed trigger's run
parameters. It is in scope and was being dropped, so nothing downstream could
name what destroyed the permanent.
